-From 0112f4234863191526afdcefd0bf89f5d913fe4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
-Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:55:12 +0000
-Subject: [PATCH] Add production docker-compose for self-hosting on Oracle
- Cloud Free Tier
-
-Railway's free credit ran out, so this adds a self-contained deploy
-setup for moving the backend + Postgres to an always-free VM (Oracle
-Cloud's Always Free shape, or any VM with Docker) instead of paying
-for Railway Hobby.
-
-deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml runs three containers: Postgres
-(seeded from Backend/sql on first start via docker-entrypoint-initdb.d),
-the Spring Boot backend (built from the existing Backend/Dockerfile,
-same DATABASE_URL/JWT_SECRET/CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS env vars it already
-reads), and Caddy as a reverse proxy that auto-provisions and renews
-a Let's Encrypt TLS cert for BACKEND_DOMAIN - needed because the
-Vercel frontend is served over HTTPS and browsers block a plain-HTTP
-API call from an HTTPS page. No backend code changes were needed;
-this is purely new deploy config.
-
-deploy/.env.example documents the variables to fill into deploy/.env
-(gitignored) before running `docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml
-up -d --build` on the VM. Includes a note about the sslip.io trick
-for getting Caddy a real cert without owning a domain (e.g.
-"1-2-3-4.sslip.io" resolves to 1.2.3.4).
-
-Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
-Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X9yZ7cHnDzcjxUURarrjHg
