-From 97bb8bfd55f9139fb88cb4794dbea449403888af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
-Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 11:20:21 +0000
-Subject: [PATCH] Tune docker-compose memory limits for VM.Standard.E2.1.Micro
- (1GB RAM)
-
-A1.Flex was out of capacity, so the target VM is the older x86 Always
-Free shape instead - 1 OCPU / 1GB RAM. Without limits, Postgres +
-Spring Boot + Caddy together can exceed that and get OOM-killed, and
-the JVM in particular sizes its default heap as a fraction of visible
-container memory rather than something safe for 1GB total.
-
-- mem_limit per service (postgres 300m, backend 500m, caddy 100m)
-  leaves headroom under 1GB for the OS and swap spikes.
-- Postgres started with shared_buffers=64MB, max_connections=20,
-  work_mem=4MB instead of its defaults (sized for far more RAM).
-- Backend gets JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS capping heap/metaspace/thread stack
-  size explicitly, since leaving it to JVM ergonomics risks an OOM
-  kill during startup class loading.
-
-Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
-Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X9yZ7cHnDzcjxUURarrjHg
